    en: "Algiers Opera House is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Algeria. The Algiers Opera House is a modern architectural jewel built as a gift from China to Algeria. It is the premier center for classical music and ballet in the country. Opened in 2016. Gift from China. 1,400 seats. This landmark is part of the cultural heritage of Algeria, reflecting Berber, Arab and Mediterranean influences. Like many notable places in Algeria, it combines Berber heritage with Mediterranean and Saharan influences. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Algeria."
